 148:main.c        **** 
 149:main.c        **** //a/o v51: There've been some unusual testing in here...
 150:main.c        **** //         e.g. one of the first experiments was to use a dual-pixel
 151:main.c        **** //         display *directly* with the single-pixel GPU. Thus, the
 152:main.c        **** //         horizontal resolution, according to the computer, was 1/2 the 
 153:main.c        **** //			  physical resolution of the screen...
 154:main.c        **** //         Later, this display was connected via a single-to-dual pixel
 155:main.c        **** //         converter. At this point, the EDID information shouldn't rely in
 156:main.c        **** //         any way on the fact that the display is a dual-pixel display
GAS LISTING /tmp/ccndhrDO.s 			page 6


 157:main.c        **** //         since it looks like a single-pixel display to the computer.
 158:main.c        **** //         But the weird math remains here.
 159:main.c        **** //         As a result of these strange tests, there's some weird stuff in
 160:main.c        **** //         here regarding H_RES and PIX_CLK_OVERRIDE, etc.
 161:main.c        **** //         I haven't yet removed it.
 162:main.c        **** // e.g. As it's currently configured...
 163:main.c        **** //      (note that _LTD is referring to my LTD121... LCD. NOT "limited")
