 626:main.c        **** //E-EDID:
 627:main.c        **** //Notes regarding EDID Monitor Range Limits Descriptor:
 628:main.c        **** //		Use of this descriptor is mandatory. 
 629:main.c        **** //		Any timing outside these limits may cause the monitor to enter a 
 630:main.c        **** //		self-protection mode. The host shall always verify that an intended 
 631:main.c        **** //		timing falls within these limits before the timing is applied.
 632:main.c        **** // My Notes:
 633:main.c        **** //  This does not seem to be implemented in any of the displays 
 634:main.c        **** //  I've checked.
 635:main.c        **** //  Nor is it mentioned in SPWG
 636:main.c        **** //But E-EDID mentions it twice!
 637:main.c        **** // 1) All blocks shall be filled with valid data using the formats
 638:main.c        **** //		described in sections 3.10.2 and 3.10.3.  Use of a data 
 639:main.c        **** //		fill pattern is not permitted. 
 640:main.c        **** // 2) Timing data must represent a supported mode of the display. 
 641:main.c        **** //	3) Descriptor blocks shall be ordered such that all detailed timing
 642:main.c        **** //		blocks precede other  types of descriptor blocks 
 643:main.c        **** //	4) The first descriptor block shall be used to indicate the display's
 644:main.c        **** //		preferred timing mode.  This is described in section 3.10.1 
 645:main.c        **** //	5) A Monitor Range Limits Descriptor must be provided 
 646:main.c        **** //	6) A Monitor Name Descriptor must be provided 
 647:main.c        **** //Note:  Items 4, 5 and 6 above were permitted but not required prior to 
 648:main.c        **** //		EDID structure version 1 revision 3.  Hosts may encounter displays 
 649:main.c        **** //		using EDID version 1 revision 0-2 which do not meet all of these 
 650:main.c        **** //		requirements.
 651:main.c        **** // Yeah, but All the screens I've checked report to be EDID V1R3...
